---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Aims & Scope — Lex Research International Law Journal"
  description="Lex Research publishes peer-reviewed, open-access scholarship in international law, human rights, IHL, comparative law, and 15 specialist fields. Read our aims and scope."
  keywords="aims and scope, international law journal, open access, peer reviewed, submission scope, legal scholarship, Lex Research"
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-slate-900 text-white py-16 sm:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- decorative grid lines -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.04]" style="background-image: linear-gradient(#f59e0b 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, #f59e0b 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 48px 48px;"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-2 rounded-full mb-6">
        Journal Policy
      </div>
      <h1 class="serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 leading-tight">
        Aims &amp; Scope
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-light max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        What Lex Research sets out to do, what we publish, who we publish it for, and the standards every article must meet before it appears on this journal.
      </p>
      <!-- quick stats bar -->
      <div class="mt-10 inline-flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-300"><span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 inline-block flex-shrink-0"></span>15 Specialist Fields</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-300"><span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 inline-block flex-shrink-0"></span>Open Access, Always</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-300"><span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 inline-block flex-shrink-0"></span>Peer Reviewed</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-300"><span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 inline-block flex-shrink-0"></span>Founded 2026</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-20 space-y-16 sm:space-y-24">

    <!-- ── Aims ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Our Aims</div>
      <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6 max-w-xl">
        Making rigorous legal scholarship accessible to everyone who needs it
      </h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {[
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3.055 11H5a2 2 0 012 2v1a2 2 0 002 2 2 2 0 012 2v2.945M8 3.935V5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0010.5 8h.5a2 2 0 012 2 2 2 0 104 0 2 2 0 012-2h1.064M15 20.488V18a2 2 0 012-2h3.064"/>`,
            title: 'Global Accessibility',
            body: 'All articles are freely accessible to every reader, everywhere, without subscription, institutional login, or payment. International law shapes lives worldwide — the scholarship that explains it must be equally reachable.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/>`,
            title: 'Scholarly Rigour',
            body: 'Every article is grounded in primary sources — treaty text, judicial decisions, UN instruments, and peer-reviewed scholarship. Analysis must meet the standards of legal academia, not legal commentary or advocacy.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z"/>`,
            title: 'Intellectual Honesty',
            body: 'Where the law is disputed, where state practice diverges from treaty text, or where courts have reached conflicting results, we say so clearly. Authoritative-sounding writing that obscures legal uncertainty has no place here.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"/>`,
            title: 'Serving the Field',
            body: 'We publish to serve law students, practitioners, academics, policymakers, and civil society organisations who need accurate and fully cited international law analysis — not to generate profit or institutional prestige.',
          },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="flex gap-4 items-start p-5 rounded-2xl bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 hover:border-amber-200 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" set:html={item.icon} />
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1.5">{item.title}</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Scope / Fields ────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Scope of Coverage</div>
      <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Fifteen specialist fields. One editorial standard.</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-7 mb-8 max-w-2xl">
        Lex Research covers international and comparative law in breadth and depth. The fifteen fields below represent the boundaries of our editorial scope. Submissions that fall clearly outside these areas will not be accepted.
      </p>

      <!-- Primary six (large cards) -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
        {[
          { emoji: '🌍', color: 'amber',   title: 'World Law',                  body: 'Comparative legal systems, constitutional frameworks, and the convergence of national legal traditions across jurisdictions.' },
          { emoji: '🌊', color: 'blue',    title: 'River Law',                  body: 'Transboundary watercourse governance, freshwater rights, and the UN Watercourses Convention in an era of climate crisis.' },
          { emoji: '🏛️', color: 'emerald', title: 'International Law',          body: 'Treaty regimes, sovereignty doctrine, customary international law, and the architecture of the UN system.' },
          { emoji: '✊', color: 'rose',    title: 'Human Rights Law',           body: 'ICCPR, ICESCR, CAT, regional instruments, and their application in capital cases, detention, and migration.' },
          { emoji: '🕊️', color: 'orange',  title: 'Humanitarian Law',           body: 'Geneva Conventions, Additional Protocols, the laws of armed conflict, and IHL compliance in modern warfare.' },
          { emoji: '⚖️', color: 'red',     title: 'International Criminal Law', body: 'ICC jurisdiction, universal jurisdiction, war crimes prosecution, and accountability of state and non-state actors.' },
        ].map(f => (
          <div class={`border border-${f.color}-200 bg-${f.color}-50 rounded-2xl p-5`}>
            <div class="text-3xl mb-3">{f.emoji}</div>
            <div class={`font-bold text-${f.color}-900 mb-2 text-sm`}>{f.title}</div>
            <p class={`text-xs text-${f.color}-800 leading-relaxed`}>{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <!-- Secondary nine (compact pill list) -->
      <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-stone-400 mb-4">Also within scope</div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {[
            'Trade Law', 'Environmental Law', 'Maritime Law',
            'Investment Law', 'Diplomatic Law', 'Refugee Law',
            'Labour Law', 'Intellectual Property Law', 'Property Law',
          ].map(f => (
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white border border-stone-200 text-xs font-medium text-slate-700">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400 inline-block"></span>
              {f}
            </span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Types of article accepted ───────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Article Types</div>
      <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">What we publish</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            n: '01',
            title: 'Doctrinal Analysis',
            body: 'Systematic examination of a legal rule, instrument, or doctrine — its text, judicial interpretation, and interaction with other legal obligations. This is the core article type at Lex Research and the benchmark against which all submissions are assessed.',
          },
          {
            n: '02',
            title: 'Comparative Studies',
            body: 'Rigorous comparison of how two or more legal systems or jurisdictions approach a shared problem, with analysis of divergence, convergence, and what each approach achieves in practice.',
          },
          {
            n: '03',
            title: 'Case Commentaries',
            body: 'In-depth analysis of a significant international court or tribunal decision — its reasoning, its relationship to prior jurisprudence, and its implications for the development of the law. Suitable for landmark ICJ, ICC, ECHR, or IACtHR rulings.',
          },
          {
            n: '04',
            title: 'Treaty & Instrument Analysis',
            body: 'Focused examination of a treaty, convention, protocol, or UN instrument: its negotiating history, drafting ambiguities, ratification record, reservations made, and how it has been applied by courts, committees, and states in practice.',
          },
          {
            n: '05',
            title: 'Critical & Socio-Legal Analysis',
            body: 'Scholarship that interrogates how international legal rules operate in context — who benefits, who bears the burden, where enforcement fails, and how structural inequalities shape the application of law. Must remain grounded in primary legal sources.',
          },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="flex gap-5 items-start p-5 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 hover:border-amber-200 transition-colors">
            <div class="text-2xl font-black text-stone-200 flex-shrink-0 leading-none mt-0.5 w-8 text-center">{item.n}</div>
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1.5">{item.title}</div>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Geographic & Jurisdictional Scope ─────────── -->
    <section class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Geographic Scope</div>
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">No jurisdiction excluded</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-7 mb-4">
          Lex Research imposes no geographic restriction on subject matter. Articles may engage with legal systems, courts, and state practice from any region — Asia-Pacific, the Americas, Africa, Europe, the Middle East, or multilateral institutions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-7">
          We actively seek scholarship that addresses under-represented legal systems and non-Western jurisprudential traditions. The dominance of European and North American perspectives in international legal scholarship is a structural problem the journal works to correct.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Language</div>
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">English only, for now</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-7 mb-4">
          All published articles appear in English. This is an operational constraint of the current editorial team, not a statement of preference. Submissions originally drafted in another language are welcome provided they are accompanied by a competent English translation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-7">
          Authors whose primary scholarly language is not English should not be disadvantaged by stylistic irregularities alone. We assess the quality of legal reasoning, citation practice, and analytical clarity — not native fluency.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── What we do NOT publish ────────────────────── -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 text-white">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-400 mb-3">Out of Scope</div>
      <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold mb-2">What Lex Research does not publish</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-8 max-w-xl">Understanding what falls outside our scope is as important as understanding what is within it.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {[
          { title: 'Pure opinion or commentary', body: 'Articles that assert a legal or political position without doctrinal grounding in primary sources will not be accepted, regardless of the eminence of the author.' },
          { title: 'Domestic-only analysis', body: 'Articles confined to the domestic law of a single jurisdiction with no international or comparative dimension fall outside our editorial scope.' },
          { title: 'Undisclosed advocacy', body: 'Work that advances a partisan position without disclosure of the author\'s institutional or financial interest will not be published.' },
          { title: 'Unverifiable citations', body: 'Any article whose primary citations cannot be independently verified by the editorial team will be returned. Broken links, absent treaty references, and misattributed decisions are grounds for rejection.' },
          { title: 'Non-legal social science', body: 'Empirical political science, economics, or sociology articles with only tangential legal content are outside scope, even where they reference international instruments.' },
          { title: 'News reporting', body: 'Lex Research does not publish journalism, press releases, or commentary on current events. If an article relies primarily on news sources rather than legal instruments and judicial decisions, it is not suitable.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="flex gap-4 items-start p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <div class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full border-2 border-red-400/60 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              <svg class="w-2.5 h-2.5 text-red-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="3" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-white text-sm mb-1">{item.title}</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Readership ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-600 mb-3">Readership</div>
      <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">Written for people who need it to be right</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        {[
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 14l9-5-9-5-9 5 9 5z"/><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 14l6.16-3.422a12.083 12.083 0 01.665 6.479A11.952 11.952 0 0012 20.055a11.952 11.952 0 00-6.824-2.998 12.078 12.078 0 01.665-6.479L12 14z"/>`,
            title: 'Law Students',
            body: 'Doctrinal analysis with full citations, case law references, and treaty text to support coursework and independent research.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 13.255A23.931 23.931 0 0112 15c-3.183 0-6.22-.62-9-1.745M16 6V4a2 2 0 00-2-2h-4a2 2 0 00-2 2v2m4 6h.01M5 20h14a2 2 0 002-2V8a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z"/>`,
            title: 'Legal Practitioners',
            body: 'Concise analysis of treaty obligations, ICJ jurisprudence, and state practice for international mandates and cross-border litigation.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 20l-5.447-2.724A1 1 0 013 16.382V5.618a1 1 0 011.447-.894L9 7m0 13l6-3m-6 3V7m6 10l4.553 2.276A1 1 0 0021 18.382V7.618a1 1 0 00-.553-.894L15 4m0 13V4m0 0L9 7"/>`,
            title: 'Academics',
            body: 'Peer-reviewed scholarship with full source transparency, suitable for citation and further academic development.',
          },
          {
            icon: `<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3.055 11H5a2 2 0 012 2v1a2 2 0 002 2 2 2 0 012 2v2.945M8 3.935V5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0010.5 8h.5a2 2 0 012 2 2 2 0 104 0 2 2 0 012-2h1.064M15 20.488V18a2 2 0 012-2h3.064"/>`,
            title: 'Policymakers',
            body: 'Rigorous analysis of international legal obligations, state compliance records, and available accountability mechanisms.',
          },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 p-5 rounded-2xl bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 hover:border-amber-200 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors">
            <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" set:html={item.icon} />
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1.5">{item.title}</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Open Access Statement ─────────────────────── -->
    <section class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="text-4xl flex-shrink-0">🔓</div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-700 mb-2">Open Access Policy</div>
          <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Open access is not a feature. It is the foundation.</h2>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm leading-7 mb-3">
            Lex Research was established on the principle that legal scholarship must be freely accessible to everyone who needs it — practitioners in jurisdictions with no law school libraries, students unable to afford journal subscriptions, advocates working in civil society with no institutional affiliation. Every article published on this journal is, and will remain, free to read.
          </p>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm leading-7">
            We do not charge article processing fees (APCs). We do not charge readers. We do not place content behind embargoes. Open access is not conditional on funding, geography, or institutional affiliation. It applies without exception.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-10 text-center">
      <div class="text-3xl mb-4">⚖️</div>
      <h3 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Read the scholarship</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm sm:text-base mb-8 max-w-md mx-auto">Browse peer-reviewed analysis across fifteen fields of international and comparative law — freely accessible, fully cited, updated continuously.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
        <a href="/articles" class="bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-400 text-slate-900 font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-xl text-sm transition-colors">Browse Articles</a>
        <a href="/about" class="bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-xl text-sm transition-colors border border-slate-700">About the Journal</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

</Base>
